KZ3 patch 1076 (SPU pass 59): KZ3_JM_DEP=1, an opt-in probe (default off, no effect when unset) of the WWS job
manager's job list under the per-SPU kernel (patch 1074, KZ3_SPURS_KERNEL=1), written to find why KZ3's first
jm_generic list (wid 8) strands at boot with 1074 + 1062. Lines tagged [jmdep]:
- ppu-ready: the PPU's ReadyCount imports (first 20 per wid), with the old and new byte.
- ready: an instance ready byte changed by an SPU PUTLLC (wid 8 always, 30 per other wid), with SPU, r0, LS 0x1500.
- empty: a module run whose AllocateJob found nothing (LS 0x1440 = 0): LS 0x14E0, LS 0x14C0 and the PM's 16-entry
  line copy at LS 0xD00 ({u16 size, u16 type, u32 ea}); entries of type != 0/1/3/4 are recorded as dependency words.
- dep: a recorded dependency word changed by an SPU commit; tick: every 2 s, the recorded words and wid 8's ready
  count and contention, and the jm_generic list (below).
- list run / list tick: the list header line (EA from the PM's LS 0x1410), t = [hdr+8], entries [hdr+0x30+4t], the
  t cursor quad hdr+0x40+16t {u16 high-water, u16 cursor, u16 per-SPU in-flight[6]} and 16 slots from cursor - 4.
- hdr-commit (KZ3_JM_DEP_HDR=<hex header EA>): every SPU commit on that header line: the cursor quad after it, the PM's
  cached entry-line EA (LS 0x14C0) and the slot it just passed, as the PM's LS copy and as memory.
- spu-put: SPU DMA PUTs into [header, header + 0x100) (g_spu_put_hook, chained).
Layouts: the RE notes Pass 59 (static read of the PM at EA 0x012BF080 and of the PPU list functions 0xA78648,
0xA7859C, 0xA786E0, 0xA78E54, 0xA79590, 0xA79A08, 0xA79A98).

